{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion","id":1335564,"title":"Aeon Aexpansion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-13T11:50:54-07:00","id":1335564,"title":"Aeon Aexpansion","content":"The Aeon Aexpansion pdf was just made available. I downloaded it and read through the Superior and Psiad sections immediately -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SNLJDR-XbVY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SNLJDR-XbVY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SNLJDR-XbVY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SNLJDR-XbVY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah. It's that amazing.<br /> <br /> I don't think there is anything, at all, in either the Superior or Psiad section that I don't like. That had me go &quot;nah&quot; that had me go &quot;I'm gonna change that&quot;. From stats to powers to general fluff. ITS BRILLIANT!!!!!!!!!!<br /> <br /> Psiads are amazing. Psiads are spectacular. Psiads are what I wanted them to beeeeeeeee!<br /> <br /> I don't think I'm ever going to play a Psion when I can play an awesome natural Psiad. Yep. I'm hooked.<br /> <br /> On Superiors. Now I don't know if that is how Stalwarts will be but till we get Adventure! era characters Superiors are the perfect, PERFECT I SAY, form of that. Their physical, mental, social power categories* are brilliant and awesome. EVERY power had me going &quot;Oh cool&quot; and &quot;oh awesome&quot;.<br /> <br /> I honestly really want to play a world where its just Superiors as I think that would be a very VERY fantastic way to go about it. (A part of me would like for some Talent Gifts to be brought over to Superiors, but in all honestly that might not even be necessary upon a more indepth reading.)<br /> <br /> *One think I think might be needed is to have Superior powers be labeled as something. Be it Knack or Gift or something else. I like power categories and 'Superior Powers' is not as cool as saying &quot;I'm manifesting a Knack&quot;.<br /> <br /> I LOVE it, in all ways. I honestly don't think I can state it anymore.<br /> <br /> ...going back to the file to continue reading it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 09-13-2019, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T11:50:10-07:00","id":1335563,"title":"","content":"The Aexpansion is out to backers. I jumped right to the aberrants and their cults. One thing I noticed is dice pools are bigger in the Aexpansion than in the Aeon antagonist section. Looks like I need to beef up the Nemesis I put together for my game starting tonight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T11:57:53-07:00","id":1335565,"title":"","content":"Cool Cool Cool downloaded and opening now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T12:03:02-07:00","id":1335568,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it really is cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To add to my gushing I also LOVE the chapter on Psions in the Modern Day. Its got such a fantastic amount of potentially awesome ideas. Which is brilliant. And Awesome. <br /> <br /> Oooooooooh as another note the ART in the book is Brilliant. Especially the tech and vehicle stuff. But everything else as well. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T12:12:41-07:00","id":1335570,"title":"","content":"The art is beautiful, gives the perfect sense of the life in 2120s, the bioarchologies and all the things... awesome.<br /> <br /> The rules for Psiads and Superiors are fantastic. I loved the way ALL Psiads in aeon era are potential QKs and the way it compensates the versatility with limited maximum power, also the one mode you can have another dot as an edge.<br /> Superiors are awesome, very versatile and at same time focused on what we could call Mega Attributes and Mega Edges on a lower scale.<br /> <br /> Now, I will read it properly (the old Aberrant books will have to wait)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T12:17:08-07:00","id":1335572,"title":"","content":"The one thing I would change is that at higher Psi a Psiad would be able to unlock higher modes dots. But that isn't so much a 'failure' in the rules as a logical element of humanity's current genetic slash noetic level. But yeah, if I was in a game and my players had Psi 6 and such I could totally see saying &quot;after some campaign act raising Psi to 7 would allow mod e to go 5/4, etc&quot; <br /> <br /> But yeah Psiads and Superiors are fantastic. <br /> <br /> The whole potential QK is not something that I imagined but it is something I love. <br /> <br /> I really think the whole lower sacle nature of Superior powers is brilliant. Its like you can see where they can go to even as they are not their yet. <br /> <br /> Its also like they are mini-Exalted. I'm a fan. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T12:21:02-07:00","id":1335575,"title":"","content":"As I said in my thread, I noticed the beefed up the antagonists in the Aberrant section. Everyone is rocking a few more dice in each pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T13:03:44-07:00","id":1335585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335575#post1335575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said in my thread, I noticed the beefed up the antagonists in the Aberrant section. Everyone is rocking a few more dice in each pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is due to changes made in the final versions of Core and Aeon, probably made after much of (if not all) the text were finished. They made it is a way you roll less dice and add more enhancements (and scale) what didn\u2019t happen before.<br /> <br /> I would stay on the dice pools described in Core and Aeon, they are enough if you use the enhancements as described there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T13:11:05-07:00","id":1335587,"title":"","content":"Another of the things I love about Superiprs is that their Powers have dot ratings. Which mean potential for growth and expansion. <br /> <br /> I do wish there was a small section on &quot;What Superior Powers Cover&quot; and &quot;How to form Superior Powers&quot; like there is about Talent Gifts in the Core. <br /> <br /> BUT thats not really a negative. Especially cause of how awesome the powers are. Like seriously. <br /> <br /> Funny enough the character I was thinking up as a Nova fits a bit better as a Superior. Maybe with one or two special powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 09-13-2019, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T14:32:55-07:00","id":1335604,"title":"","content":"Loving it so far. Once I have a chance to sit down with it, I'm probably going to do a compare and contrast between Superiors, Aberrant Cults, and TC:Ab. (I haven't yet read either of the Quantum-powered sections in detail yet, so I can't comment yet.)<br /> <br /> I love the idea that all psiads are potential quantakinetics, and the implications that has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T15:11:46-07:00","id":1335615,"title":"","content":"AExpansion was in layout before the final changes were made to Core downgrading antagonist dicepools. As such, those numbers in AExpansion may change before final.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T15:24:40-07:00","id":1335617,"title":"","content":"LOVE LOVE LOVE the Akiyama Group and definitely treating them as a full Allegiance option for Superior characters (the rules currently make them an Origin Path).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m less sure about how I feel about the Aeon Society having the Nakamura Procedure, and may have Hamdan and Mizuki working on it still at my own table - something Nippon spies will do anything to stop and FSA agents scheme to steal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T15:33:05-07:00","id":1335618,"title":"","content":"I think giving Aeon the ability is too allow for maximum player possibilities as not everyone who wants to play a Superior would want to be from Nippon. That said as of the present there are fifteen Aeon Superors*,<br /> <br /> *My opinion is that instead of giving such a number the book should say something like &quot;a few dozen&quot; or &quot;a score&quot; or something. Just my opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T15:37:56-07:00","id":1335620,"title":"","content":"Just reading this now - Loving the VARG section. I do wonder why VARG's are not just made Scale 2/3 instead of 1/2 when they add an additional +2 enhancment on size related rolls anyway. Plus the image on page 48 looks much larger tha I would class size 2... <br /> <br /> Still - book is great. Really enjoying it so far. Packed full of good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T19:49:14-07:00","id":1335646,"title":"","content":"By the way as I read the Superiors I can't help but think that Tony Stark would better be statted up as a natural born Superior than a full on Nova. The powers of the Superiors basically fit him better I think. A part of this is that the hypothetical player of a Tony Stark like character would be able to have things to purchase as the game progresses. <br /> <br /> Yeah, as I read over the Superiors chapter, the Psiad chapter, the Psions in the Modern World chapter I can't help but love it more and more. Power write up, descriptive fluff, mechanical nature, setting ideas, all are brilliant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T20:00:50-07:00","id":1335648,"title":"","content":"I thought Nippon still had some carefully controlled Novas ALONG with Superiors and apparently Talents? Or was that only a 1e thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T21:23:01-07:00","id":1335656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335648#post1335648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Nippon still had some carefully controlled Novas ALONG with Superiors and apparently Talents? Or was that only a 1e thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just 1e (well not even technically 1e, since Asia Ascended isn\u2019t technically published canon, but it would have been). The last of the Nihjon Novas died defending the Solar System from Colony in 2105.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T21:46:19-07:00","id":1335657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335646#post1335646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way as I read the Superiors I can't help but think that Tony Stark would better be statted up as a natural born Superior than a full on Nova.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stark\u2019s genius goes way beyond what a Superior can achieve. Guy goes from building an impossible power source and armour in a cave, to super-versatile nanotech, to cracking time travel, within a 15-ish year period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T22:06:35-07:00","id":1335659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335657#post1335657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stark\u2019s genius goes way beyond what a Superior can achieve. Guy goes from building an impossible power source and armour in a cave, to super-versatile nanotech, to cracking time travel, within a 15-ish year period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But mechanically he is lacking most Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges, and all powers. Which means on a player level he will lack a lot of stuff to purchase. If he gets statted as say a Superior I could see a player mechanically purchasing a number of different Superior Powers. Which lets the player buy stuff. Which is why I think mechanically something like this works better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T22:14:43-07:00","id":1335662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335657#post1335657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stark\u2019s genius goes way beyond what a Superior can achieve. Guy goes from building an impossible power source and armour in a cave, to super-versatile nanotech, to cracking time travel, within a 15-ish year period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, though he may qualify as a \u201cstealth nova\u201d, with \u201conly\u201d two or three dots of Mega-Intelligence. On the other hand, Spitfire (from the original New Universe) might easily be a Superior who invented a VARG a century ahead of time. <br /> <br /> On another note, I wonder if Superiors can be thought of as a preview of TC:A!'s Stalwarts\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T22:19:01-07:00","id":1335664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335659#post1335659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. But mechanically he is lacking most Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges, and all powers. Which means on a player level he will lack a lot of stuff to purchase. If he gets statted as say a Superior I could see a player mechanically purchasing a number of different Superior Powers. Which lets the player buy stuff. Which is why I think mechanically something like this works better.</div> </div> </div> </div>TC:Ab has stealth novas in it (I think they're now called Dark Stars) who are novas who lack most Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges, and all powers. Stark is a Nova rather than a Superior not just because he wasn't artificially produced by Nippon but also because he clearly has Mega-Intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T23:55:45-07:00","id":1335675,"title":"","content":"So I'm not sure I get the point of the &quot;More powered People&quot; sidebar on page 82. Wouldn't they also be psiads?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T00:12:33-07:00","id":1335679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335675#post1335675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm not sure I get the point of the &amp;quot;More powered People&amp;quot; sidebar on page 82. Wouldn't they also be psiads?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they lack the ability to store Psi points of their own. By definition they wouldn\u2019t be psiads, but their powers might look very similar if they had any way of powering them. Or they might not, as the reservoir used to power their abilities might be \u2018flavoured\u2019 to only work for certain Aptitudes or combinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T01:02:22-07:00","id":1335683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335679#post1335679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they lack the ability to store Psi points of their own. By definition they wouldn\u2019t be psiads, but their powers might look very similar if they had any way of powering them. Or they might not, as the reservoir used to power their abilities might be \u2018flavoured\u2019 to only work for certain Aptitudes or combinations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right I mean I'm not sure what they would look like and how they would be different much from other types currently?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T01:23:49-07:00","id":1335686,"title":"","content":"And at this stage, no one knows. We\u2019re just opening the door a little...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T06:48:01-07:00","id":1335716,"title":"","content":"Would it be correct to say that Captain America is a superior?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T07:21:35-07:00","id":1335721,"title":"","content":"Rather then debating in circle the issue non-issue of Tony Statk I'm gonna ask inatead if anyone has any thoughts on the now revealed rules for Superiors and Psiads? <br /> <br /> As I said I really like them both. <br /> <br /> For Psiads the fact all gain QK is like woah, but I like that addition to the lore. That and all Aptitudes are available and the fact that highed Psi might mean higher mode maxes. <br /> <br /> For Superiors I really like how the powers are described and given stats. The fact multiple levels exist give so many options. I can also see where in another time and place of development the powers would become more. <br /> <br /> I do wonder if the restrictions on only effecting the self mentioned here are artificial ones that Stalwarts would not have to worry about. Still till we get Stalwart rules I could see using the mechanics of Superiors quite easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T08:02:32-07:00","id":1335724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335716#post1335716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be correct to say that Captain America is a superior?</div> </div> </div> </div>Narratively - definitely. Power level wise varies massively depending on the continuity and current author. Superior might be the average though between him being an exceptionally statted baseline (or Nova entirely invested in mundane Attributes and Abilities) or someone with full blown Mega-Presence and at least 1 dot in each of the Mega-Physicals as he is in the MCU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-14-2019, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T08:16:51-07:00","id":1335727,"title":"","content":"As someone <i>maybe</i> interested in this product - <b>Can someone run down me general view on how Psions, Psiads and Superiors are different from each other?</b> It can only be in general lore description, but pointing some broad mechanics differences would also help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T08:44:20-07:00","id":1335731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335727#post1335727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone <i>maybe</i> interested in this product - <b>Can someone run down me general view on how Psions, Psiads and Superiors are different from each other?</b> It can only be in general lore description, but pointing some broad mechanics differences would also help.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Psiads - These are individuals who have naturally come into their noetic/psychic abilities. Because of this they generally have a lower power maximum while making it up by being able to learn powers from all psychic Aptitudes. They are what one should be when accessing noetic power. <br /> <br /> Psions - These are individuals who have gained access to their psychic/noetic powers thanks to an artificial process known as the Prometheus Effect. They gain greater power maximums at the restriction of only knowing one Aptitude of psychic power. They are artificial in that the technology that makes them available is alien. <br /> <br /> Both Psiads and Psions use the same listing of Psychic Aptitudes and Modes so in this they are the same. The main difference is, as stated, Psiads are not restricted to a single Aptitude while Psions are. That said at the current standpoint of human evolution Psiads are limited to Aptitude 4 in primary and 3 in secondary while Psions can go up much higher in their chosen Aptitude. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Superiors - Are individuals associated with Quantum energies given manifestation through a Nippon-made but Aeon-gained technological process. Their powers are organized as either Physical, Mental, or Social and are much lower powered then their Nova super brethren. Their powers control the self but are limited in being able to control others or the world. This limitation is in some ways artificial, though that said it is intrinsic to being a Superior. <br /> <br /> Psiads and Psions use Noetic energy while Superiors (and Novas) use Quantum energy. <br /> <br /> I hope this helps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T09:35:21-07:00","id":1335738,"title":"","content":"Put another way, Superiors are \u201cartificial Novas\u201d in the same way that Psions are \u201cartificial Psiads\u201d and, like Psions, they have their potential range of abilities greatly restricted compared to their natural counterparts: a Superior only gets inwardly-directed powers (basically, a subset of TC:Ab's Mega-Edges; no Quantum Powers) and have to focus on physical, mental, or social abilities (though not to the exclusion of the other two); <i>and</i> they don't get Mega-Attributes. So in their case, the tradeoff isn't diversity for power as it is with Psions. Rather, it's diversity for stability: Superiors don't ever have to worry about Flux or Transcendence or their TC:\u00c6 equivalent.<br /> <br /> In fact, that's the whole point of creating a Superior: it eliminates the possibility the he or she might ever spontaneously Erupt and become an Aberrant monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-14-2019, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T09:56:07-07:00","id":1335739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335620#post1335620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just reading this now - Loving the VARG section. I do wonder why VARG's are not just made Scale 2/3 instead of 1/2 when they add an additional +2 enhancment on size related rolls anyway. Plus the image on page 48 looks much larger tha I would class size 2...</div> </div> </div> </div>Size Scale is tremendous different from the sizes in DnD, I don\u2019t think you are comparing, but I had to make this comparison.<br /> <br /> Size 1 is basically human sized. Hulk in full power is Size 1, Veronica armor from Age of Ultron is Size 1.<br /> <br /> Size 2 is huge. A car is Size 2, a truck is size 2, a buss, even a small plane is size 2, all the transformers, including Optimus Prime are Size 2.<br /> <br /> Size 3 is even bigger. To be size 3 it must fit like a hundred people inside easily, like a 747 or bigger, the largest airplanes are all size 3, most of the warships are size 3, Castles are size 3. I would say Godzilla on most of the movies is Size 3, the Kaijus and Jagers from Pacific Rim are all size 3. Size 3 creature with legs is the limit of impossible in real world, at least on our gravity, the legs must be huge to hold the weight, the few creatures size 3 are whales and maybe the largest dinosaurs, just because of the long necks and tails, not because the body itself.<br /> <br /> Size 4 is something as big as a Cruiser ship, Aircraft Carrier, a Freighter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T10:01:11-07:00","id":1335741,"title":"","content":"Having just reread the Psiad rules from 1e, I was delightfully surprised by how different the new rules are. While I was somewhat partial to the pairings of the Mental, Physical, and Energetic modes from 1e, the developments around QK are quite nice.<br /> <br /> I also really like the balance struck between Psions and Psiads, while the flavor text was really making the case for Psiads (I mean, it was their section, it should be), the fact that only Psions can achieve dots 5 6 and 7 affirms their place in the setting. Also the psi-cooperation rules are still much better for Psions, at least at first blush. I'll need to really dig in to what the Psi bonus lets them accomplish together.<br /> <br /> I was worried that I was too hype for this book, but it has delivered and then some. The best thing a book can do- give me exactly what I wanted and then a bunch of things I had no idea I could have wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T10:35:03-07:00","id":1335747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335741#post1335741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was worried that I was too hype for this book, but it has delivered and then some. The best thing a book can do- give me exactly what I wanted and then a bunch of things I had no idea I could have wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same worry, and same surprise with the results.<br /> <br /> About the Psion/Psiad relation, I agree with you, they are far more powerful, not only for the higher dots, but also for the Psi points. Psiads are versatile, but they have much more difficulty to learn new powers, and have a limited use of the powers.<br /> <br /> Finally, the QK thing is, awesome the way it was described. QK is the natural human power and it\u2019s what make the Psiads shine in a universe of little Quantakinetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T10:59:03-07:00","id":1335754,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Aeon Aexpansion the hype is real and the result is glorious.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> On the restriction on Psiads with higher Mode dots I totally get it, I even approve of it on a setting level. That said if I was to run a game with Psiads and we got to the point where my players had Psi 6 I would basically have a campaign event occur that would let them gain higher mode levels at higher Psi ranks. This could be something adventure wise or it could be sneaking into a Psi Order and use a Prometheus Chamber that they recalibrated slightly so that their genetics could be enhanced.<br /> <br /> BUT, all that said, as an official rule I cannot say I have any issue with the whole limiting how high a Psiad can go considering how wide they can go.<br /> <br /> The whole QK being a natural human power is just so BRILLIANT. Like woah, how cool.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> So Superiors have no powers that effect the world outside their own being but it makes me wonder if a Power that relates to say pheremones or whatever could be applicable. Its natural and self-generated and so it still fits the theme.<br /> <br /> As an aside I wonder how much of the Superior design we will see when it comes to Stalwarts. While I would totally enjoy a slight broadening of Stalwart power theme I have to say I REALLY (like REALLY REALLY) hope that the whole idea of powers being specific things with multiple dot ratings is a thing. I LOVE that.<br /> <br /> For many reasons, one of which is the idea that a character might start off with say 1 dot in a power and that as the campaign progresses that goes to 2, then 3, and then 4, and then 5 near the end. Its the same power but it just gets progressively more developed and potent. I LOVE that concept.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Oh and I love the powers that Superiors have that basically lets them go into the wilderness, use various materials around them, and built some tools that let them build other tools that would let them build civilization. That's a brilliant thing to me.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Here is another question - Do you think Superiors would have access to powers that let them increase Scale for actions. Their powers, though constrained and limited, are somewhat proto-Nova and it would be nifty to see certain small effects related to what they could have become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 09-14-2019, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T11:50:32-07:00","id":1335760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335648#post1335648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Nippon still had some carefully controlled Novas ALONG with Superiors and apparently Talents? Or was that only a 1e thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might still be a 2e thing; but if so, it's an exception to policy. What happens when they don't get to a potential superhuman before he Erupts? You can either kill him or carefully control him. The first is a \u201cbetter safe than sorry\u201d case, while the second might happen if for whatever reason they end up not wanting to kill the new Nova. <br /> <br /> But the carefully controlled Nova is the result of a failure (to get to him before he Erupted), and there's likely to be a stigma surrounding him as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T12:38:57-07:00","id":1335768,"title":"","content":"Given how Psiads have evolved over the eras, I would expect we\u2019ll see that Mode cap go up or disappear altogether in the post-Aeon setting era when we see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T12:47:22-07:00","id":1335771,"title":"","content":"Not just that. I also expect the QK floor to drop as the psiads evolve, until psiads can develop the QK Aptitude from the start instead of having to wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T13:43:14-07:00","id":1335785,"title":"","content":"Delighted that everyone's enjoying it so far!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T14:12:40-07:00","id":1335790,"title":"","content":"Does the Kaga-2 Retrovirus effect Latents or Psi 1 Psiads?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T14:40:03-07:00","id":1335793,"title":"","content":"Latents - yes. Pre-manifestation psiads? Probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T14:48:41-07:00","id":1335797,"title":"","content":"On Kaga-2 I figure that it works on anyone not awake/aware/erupted/manifested etc. If your power is active then your safe but if your power is not then you loose stuff. <br /> <br /> That said I could totally see the campaign possibility of a person on the very momentary cusp of awakening/manifesting unconsciously using the whole nature of being given a drug as the catalyst to erupt/manifest. I would make such a manifestation/eruption a somewhat violent one as a note, one that causes irens and police presence and that is hard to hide from the news that something happened in the clinic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T15:05:51-07:00","id":1335798,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re probably safe from Kaga-2 if your power is active, but the same may not be true of Kaga-3, or -4 etc. (You know someone\u2019s developing it, right.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T15:29:27-07:00","id":1335801,"title":"","content":"And thus comes adventure hook after adventure hook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which is always brilliant. Adventure and story options are always brilliant and awesome. They help to make the world feel lively. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T15:32:40-07:00","id":1335802,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m considering a plot line focused on Earthside geopolitics instead of the interstellar conflicts the official future plotline follows that involves FSA, Russia, and the United Republic courting Nippon for access to Kaga bioweapons and maybe even the Nakamura process that will define the anti-Aeon, anti-Psi coalition in a world war if they get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-08-2020, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T15:41:22-07:00","id":1335803,"title":"","content":"Sounds fun. \ud83d\ude42<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335801#post1335801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And thus comes adventure hook after adventure hook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the plan. Check out the AEon intro fiction as well. That illegal, or at least \u2018off-the-books\u2019 lab was researching something to mess with psions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T15:59:13-07:00","id":1335804,"title":"","content":"The thing about such plans (from an inworld perspective) is that its hard for scientists to fully take into consideration all the potential methods that an active Psion can use to resist the effects either singularly or in tandem with others in cooperation. Which to me is where the fun is - such plans rarely if ever can truly be kept secret because something will let it out. Which when that happens means Aeon or the Orders will gather personnel and resources to stop the attempt. <br /> <br /> Which is as it should be. <br /> <br /> But it is also what makes the versions that work on Neutrals (even Latents) all the worse from an in-world perspective. Such people do not have metanormal abilities to resist it and so they get the drug/virius/whatever and they loose their abilities. <br /> <br /> Which is why I think it would be really cool if something happens where a person is given the drug and Erupts as either a Nova or Psiad, leading to damage in the area and a growing sense among the neutrals that maybe they should show restraint on giving these drugs to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T16:56:16-07:00","id":1335811,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed all the technology that I read so far (I started by the Super Science and VARGs).<br /> <br /> The only thing on Super Science I missed is an Inspired Noetic Device that simulate base powers. They are ignored most of the time, but it\u2019s extremely useful, imagine a Psicloak to the wearer, or a sensor that detect biosignatures at range.<br /> <br /> Edit: the tag option, I was thinking about it comparing Inspired and Advanced tech in Core. Tags are already used, so ignore that comment...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-15-2019, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T17:11:13-07:00","id":1335812,"title":"","content":"Reading up on Aberrant Cults. Need to decide if I want my villains in Securitas (FSA Insurance, Private Security, and Private Prison Megacorp that are the gov\u2019s secret police contractors literally known as the Pinkertons) to be Monolith or not....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T20:36:24-07:00","id":1335833,"title":"","content":"So am I correct in my impression of canon that Kaga-2 shuts down potential for Talent Inspiration as well, and as such Nippon simultaneously has the highest concentration of Talents as government agents thanks to the 1/6 Nakamura recipients, and the lowest concentration of Talents in the total population thanks to Kaga-2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T03:36:45-07:00","id":1335857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335833#post1335833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So am I correct in my impression of canon that Kaga-2 shuts down potential for Talent Inspiration as well, and as such Nippon simultaneously has the highest concentration of Talents as government agents thanks to the 1/6 Nakamura recipients, and the lowest concentration of Talents in the total population thanks to Kaga-2?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say Yes to the first part, and no to the second. They would have about 500 Talents in the government, what is probably the highest number in the world for sure, but if those 500 are counted on the total population, they probably have the highest in general population too.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt created many hundreds of new Talents and psiads\u201d talking about the 2104 Bhurano event. So I believe there are no more than many hundreds, maybe a few thousands in the entire world, if you think a few thousands in the world total and about 500 in Japan alone, it\u2019s still a good proportion.<br /> <br /> If you don\u2019t count the government as general population, than yes, Japan is very limited in the total of free will Talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T04:16:16-07:00","id":1335862,"title":"","content":"I want to make a point here on the way VARGs work on scale, that made me very happy with the result, by the way.<br /> <br /> VARGs can have size scale 2, but they always have a +1 scale on Durability and VARG Scale weapons babe a +1 on Power scale, it means a Size 1 has Durability 2 and possibly power 2 scale, and a Size 2 has Durability 3 and possibly power 3, not enough to fight a size 6 battle cruiser or to overwhelm any human sized weapons, but still enough to handle most of the attacks with easy.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s great for fighting Aberrants... at least those that are not too overpowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T08:07:58-07:00","id":1335892,"title":"","content":"I would like to mention that after reading the really interesting and nicely organized and written chapter on Psions in the Modern Day within Aeon Aexpansion I really hope that when we get Adventure! they include somewhere the idea of Inspired in the Modern Day where instead of N-Day causing Novas to erupt it leads to a widespread and very visible manifestation of the Inspired. Just sayin! <br /> <br /> I also thought it was amusing that also in said chapter they comment that what would happen if both Novas and Psiads manifested is beyond the scope of the book, which was amusing and also pretty accurate. <br /> <br /> But even more I liked in the whole section about Psions in the Modern Day they talk about how nothing says naturally manifesting noetic users couldn't be Psions (that is restricted to a single Aptitude) but that nothing also says a Storyteller can't use Psiads (oh and look, you know have rules for it). So that was really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T16:30:50-07:00","id":1335962,"title":"","content":"Just wondering; where did it say Superiors were Quantum-aligned. The \u00c6pansion doesn't say that, (and implies that the 1 in 4 survivors who aren't Jinketsu become Talents). I think we got the idea from the comments section of the Kickstarter but I'm concerned that was just a piece of gammon that I helped spread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T16:58:01-07:00","id":1335963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335962#post1335962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering; where did it say Superiors were Quantum-aligned. The \u00c6pansion doesn't say that, (and implies that the 1 in 4 survivors who aren't Jinketsu become Talents). I think we got the idea from the comments section of the Kickstarter but I'm concerned that was just a piece of gammon that I helped spread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... I think it\u2019s pretty obvious from literally all their mechanics that they\u2019re derived from Nova potential. It\u2019s not like it\u2019s subtle what\u2019s being played on. But i\u2019ll recheck the Aeon core about anything explicit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T17:36:26-07:00","id":1335965,"title":"","content":"They become Superiors because they had a \u201chigh\u201d probability of quantum eruption, so they should be quantum aligned.<br /> <br /> Becoming Talent is a chance of false positive as far as I would guess, or maybe Talents, Novas and Psiads have the same gene that kick the on one of the 3 directions (that is the \u201coficial\u201d answer to this since 1e).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T20:15:45-07:00","id":1335975,"title":"","content":"Can the Psiad Edges Favored Aptitude and Strong Mode be stacked for 3 Enhancement to the selected Mode, or do you get 2 Enhancement for that Mode and 1 Enhancement for the other two Modes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T22:03:42-07:00","id":1335985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335963#post1335963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean... I think it\u2019s pretty obvious from literally all their mechanics that they\u2019re derived from Nova potential. It\u2019s not like it\u2019s subtle what\u2019s being played on. But i\u2019ll recheck the Aeon core about anything explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if it was their ability to format Noetic Bioware (with rejects all Quantum users), create Noetic Bioware (a feat impossible for Quantum users), or their ability to invent new Neotic Bioware (also impossible for a Quantum user), that makes you so sure &quot;it's obvious&quot; that they use Quantum for anything?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335965#post1335965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They become Superiors because they had a \u201chigh\u201d probability of quantum eruption, so they should be quantum aligned.<br /> <br /> Becoming Talent is a chance of false positive as far as I would guess, or maybe Talents, Novas and Psiads have the same gene that kick the on one of the 3 directions (that is the \u201coficial\u201d answer to this since 1e).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in their fluff, or mechanics, ties them directly to a Quantum Origin. In fact they are selected from people that have the potential to be Inspired. This list includes: Latent PSI, and Unerupted Novas alike (and potentially Unactivated Talents). I would see the 1/4 Talents that the process creates being less a false positive, and more that the experience has a 1/4 chance to Activate Talents. (Exposure to super science is an activation condition for Talents after all.)<br /> <br /> AEon AExpansion, pg 61: &quot;These stalwart individuals are artificially created Inspired characters. Every Superior had the potential for becoming a Psion <u><i><b>or</b></i></u> a Nova, but technicians use a combination of genetic therapies, powerful drugs, and precisely controlled radiation dosages to transform them into something entirely new.&quot;<br /> <br /> *Note, I'm not saying that Superiors have nothing to do with Quantum. What I'm saying is you guys are making a lot of declarations and assumptions that just aren't supported by the currently available data.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 09-16-2019, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T23:19:38-07:00","id":1335992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335985#post1335985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if it was their ability to format Noetic Bioware (with rejects all Quantum users), create Noetic Bioware (a feat impossible for Quantum users), or their ability to invent new Neotic Bioware (also impossible for a Quantum user), that makes you so sure &quot;it's obvious&quot; that they use Quantum for anything?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that they\u2019re clearly modeled on Novas and 1e Stalwarts expression of superhumanity thematically through their attributes. Psi may be involved as a diegetic excuse for why they can use Noetic tech (a decision that strikes me as balance motivated for the Aeon Superiors\u2019 benefit, rather than thematics or setting motivated) but they\u2019re obviously modeled on being Tier 2 artifically created counterparts to Novas based on literally all their power motifs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-16-2019, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T23:22:41-07:00","id":1335994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335985#post1335985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing in their fluff, or mechanics, ties them directly to a Quantum Origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's suggested:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> AEon AExpansion, pg 61: &quot;These <u><b>stalwart</b></u> individuals are artificially created Inspired characters. Every Superior had the potential for becoming a Psion or a Nova, but technicians use a combination of genetic therapies, powerful drugs, and precisely controlled radiation dosages to transform them into something entirely new.&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T02:22:56-07:00","id":1336005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335994#post1335994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's suggested:</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that nothing in their chapter <i>directly</i> tied them to Quantum, and nothing does. In the TC Core, and in the AEon book the word &quot;Inspired&quot; in the sentence you quoted, while often used generally to refer to people with powers, it is also used to refer to Talents and their power source in particular. (ie. the Setting Secrets chapter of the TC:AEon Core) Therefore by that same logic the sentence you quoted is also a suggestion to the reader that these are in fact the artificially created version of Talents, which is far better supported in the writing then Superiors using Quantum is.<br /> <br /> Also, if we are supposed to infer that Superiors use Quantum because of the use of the word stalwart: <br /> <br /> A) Why was it decided to use a lower case adjective that means &quot;loyal and/or reliable&quot; where in it is describing beings that are usually thoroughly vetted and heavily trained government operatives to infer Quantum use instead of the upper case proper noun?<br /> <br /> and <br /> <br /> B) Why was it also chosen to do this by using the word stalwart exactly once in the thousands of words of text in the chapter, with no other facts, clues, or hints given to this relationship to Quantum?<br /> <br /> Even though: <br /> <br /> 1) Superiors have no Quantum score<br /> <br /> 2) Superiors have no Quantum points<br /> <br /> 3) In point of fact Superiors have no Power Source at all (Save for a PSI score of 1, which all non-quantum users have by nature of being alive)<br /> <br /> 4) Both artificially and naturally created PSI users are the same Tier, have the same Power Stat (PSI), have PSI points (and those points do the same things), and use very similar mechanics for their powers (PSI+Mode). While none of these facts are true when comparing Superiors to Novas.<br /> <br /> 5) The fact that a Superiors &quot;powers&quot; find themselves mirroring a Talents Gifts far more closely then anything from the Aberrant book. (You can go and check, and while they are hardly 1 for 1, the similarities are striking)<br /> <br /> 6) Artificially created PSI users, though more limited/focused, are more powerful in that focus then naturally occurring PSI users. Therefore if the artificially created Quantum users, who in theory are supposed to &quot;mirror&quot; the artificially created PSI users (in some peoples minds anyway), and therefore be the limited/focused versions of Novas... well... shouldn't that theoretical group be more powerful within that limited focus then the naturally occurring Quantum users the way that Psions are? (Think a light bulb vs a laser, both are putting out light, but the one with more focus produces increased results within it's area of effect)<br /> <br /> 7) They are able to format, create, and even invent new Noetic Biotech with the same &quot;Advanced Science only&quot; restriction as Talents. A feat that requires the individual to have a PSI rating of at least 1 per the AEon Core.<br /> <br /> After all of the above, was it really expected that one single adjective, in one single place, would suggest to the reader that Superiors were using Quantum for anything?<br /> <br /> In the end canon will be what ever it will be, but I personally feel that the Source of Superiors abilities are much better suited to be: A) The artificially created version of Talents, or B) Something new that is the result of humanities unique relationship to both Quantum, PSI, and Inspiration, or C) Undefined.<br /> <br /> I know that: 1) You're the TC Lead, and therefore have to look out for the integrity of the game line as a whole 2) Ultimately you have the final say on the nature of Superiors, and 3) What ever you say goes, but I hope that you will consider my reasons, or at the very least leave their Quantum ties as nothing more then the vague one word hint that it currently is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T03:49:59-07:00","id":1336014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335992#post1335992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that they\u2019re clearly modeled on Novas and 1e Stalwarts expression of superhumanity thematically through their attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they did this by mirroring and tweaking the effects of many Talents Gifts instead of actually doing anything directly Quantum related... right...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Psi may be involved as a diegetic excuse for why they can use Noetic tech (a decision that strikes me as balance motivated for the Aeon Superiors\u2019 benefit, rather than thematics or setting motivated) but they\u2019re obviously modeled on being Tier 2 artificially created counterparts to Novas based on literally all their power motifs. </div> </div> </div>Their power motifs are just like Novas, except they're attribute category focused instead of being specific attribute focused, oh, and they have no access to any way to customize their powers.<br /> <br /> They also have no way to effect the world beyond themselves, unlike Novas, and there's no Flux, which Novas have, and no Maxing to get powers you haven't purchased, or better version of the powers you already have, and even in the rare times you get a point of Scale (seriously, can things get any further from Novas &quot;power motifs&quot; then the inability to easily gain even a single point of Scale in any area that isn't speed or lifting related?*) there's no Collateral Pool to worry about.<br /> <br /> There's no Quantum Minimums to worry about, and no spending points to activate anything. (because you have no points to spend)<br /> <br /> They also lack power themes that you build your powers and abilities around, and lets not forget the fact that all a Superiors Powers are Innocuous by default (Unlike Novas that have to spend 24xp on every power and edge to have the Innocuous Tag), and they have powers that do things that Novas have no direct way to do**...<br /> <br /> ... yeah... except for those <i>few</i> things, <i>literally all</i> their power motifs are <i>just</i> <i>like</i> Novas...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Regardless of any official word from on high as to their vague connection to Quantum, maybe you should take a step back and compare them with their most direct counterpart, the Talents***, rather then trying to sell people on their non-existent &quot;power motif&quot; ties to Novas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Power Lifter, Speedster, and Swimming Champ are the only way to get Scale in the currently published Power list for Superiors. There are more ways to get Scale outside of their Powers (edges, skill tricks, &amp; gear), which anyone can get, then within it. Above all else <i>this</i> is what screams &quot;Not Quantum/Nova Related at All&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> **I'll admit that they things that Superiors do which Novas don't do directly are mostly covering things that Novas don't need to because they can just steam roll around or ignore the issue addressed by the Power thru superior Scale.<br /> <br /> ***Even if the Superiors are Quantum users, their most direct counterpoints are Talents: 1) They're both Tier 2 and stuck there, 2) Their Gifts and Powers have a good amount of overlap, and 3) The main difference is the Talent has outward focused abilities (Gifts/Dramatic Editing), and the Superior has inward focused Powers.<br /> <br /> In fact, the Gift list is a great place to mine for ideas when homebrewing new Powers. (Not to directly copy, but to give an idea of the appropriate power level, and to look for where they might possibly have similar effects)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T04:49:53-07:00","id":1336020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1335975#post1335975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Psiad Edges Favored Aptitude and Strong Mode be stacked for 3 Enhancement to the selected Mode, or do you get 2 Enhancement for that Mode and 1 Enhancement for the other two Modes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? I guess that\u2019s the entire idea of using both, be focused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T07:06:20-07:00","id":1336034,"title":"","content":"Far be it from me to argue with someone whose mind is made up \u2014 save, perhaps, when his mind is made up about what <i>I</i> should think. If you want to say that Superiors aren't related to the Quantum \u201caspect\u201d of whatever it is that empowers people in the Trinity Continuum, more power to you! Just don't insist that I do likewise. <br /> <br /> I mean, you're arguing with a <i>developer</i> that you hope they won't make the connection to Quantum any more explicit so that you can continue saying that there isn't an explicit connection\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T08:11:23-07:00","id":1336041,"title":"","content":"I do think that more methods of getting Scale would be useful for Superiors to have. The examples we have are all physical so I think a mental and a social Scale boost should also exist. But that said I do like the fact that Superiors don't have to spend points to use their abilities, its nifty that they just work. I really like that. <br /> <br /> I guess the thing ofr me is that I don't look at power write-ups as all inclusive and so I can invision cetain powers getting higher dot versions and new powers with their own dot versions being made as well. Because of that I look at what we see and go &quot;ooh this is a great start with some awesome writing but if I add x and add y then the powers will go more complete&quot; Which is why I have asked that we get a &quot;How to create Superior Powers&quot; sidebar like we have for Talent Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T08:15:26-07:00","id":1336042,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not going to waste my time explaining how overt superhuman attributes are thematically closer to greater scale overt superhuman attributes then either are to reality bending around skills and attributes that are never overtly superhuman, regardless of how the mechanics play out, when the developer has already confirmed that what everyone else clearly read being communicated was in fact the authorial intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T09:01:35-07:00","id":1336054,"title":"","content":"I'll say this: the rules for Talents were developed in the Core book, which everyone is assumed to have; so Talents and their Gifts are almost certainly going to be handled consistently over the entire TC line. The rules for Psi and Aptitudes were developed in \u00c6on, which was developed in tandem to the Core book; there were no prior books that included people with noetic powers. So here, too, chances are high that we're going to get a single, consistent set of rules for psionic characters throughout the entire line (though the jury's still out on how Adventure! will handle it, and I still have my hopes that we'll get something for psiads in the Nova Age that doesn't require picking up TC:\u00c6 to use). <br /> <br /> But Aberrant powers are already an anomaly in that regard, as both TC:\u00c6 and TC:Ab have published rules for them and those rules are substantially different. Yes, there are arguments that Aberrants have changed over the century since their heyday; but the changes are still there, and are substantial. So there's a fracturing of the rules where superhumans are concerned that simple isn't there (yet?) for Talents or \u201cnoetics\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T13:45:55-07:00","id":1336091,"title":"","content":"You may say Aberrant and Aeon rules are different for the description of Novas/Aberrants, but in the end they are not that different. At least in the last file (that will be print) they added scale from deviant Aberrants up, so we have possibly all the power difference between a Nova and a Psion. You can say a Nova can be much more powerful, and it\u2019s true, but you can just add another scale when needed, mainly on the Terat Archetype.<br /> <br /> The same way Aberrants added Psiads thru the view of Aberrant rules, Aeon added Superiors and Aberrants thru the view of Aeon Rules, after all, the rules for powers are massive in both books and having the other books rules would be too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T14:00:58-07:00","id":1336094,"title":"","content":"1e Aberrant added psiads through the vote of Aberrant rules; TC:Ab has not (though I'm hoping it will). But yes, I view TC:\u00c6's rules for Aberrants and Superiors as \u201chow to approximate Quantum-empowered people if you don't own TC:Ab\u201d \u2014 similar to how VtM has rules for \u201clupines\u201d for people who want to include werewolves in their games but don't own WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T14:01:33-07:00","id":1336095,"title":"","content":"One thing I would love to see on a future \u201cAbexpansion\u201d book, is a chapter for Playing Novas thru the ages, kind of the same as Psions in modern days or Psiads in general. Not rules per se, but what kind of level of power the novas and Aberrants have after a hundred years post n-day, or how much power the novas that erupted before N-Day had as a general rule (maybe a cross between Aberrant and Adventure). There\u2019s is this chapter in the old Players Guide (I was reading it before Aexpansion) about Aberrants along the history. I really enjoyed all the possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T14:19:15-07:00","id":1336097,"title":"","content":"While I do think that the Aberrant rules in Aeon are designed so as to represent Novas using Aeon rules I don't think the same of Superiors in the Aeon Aexpansion book. To me those rules ARE the rules for Superiors. The same with Psiads. To me its not a shortcut to save word count but rather a true representation of how the powers work. <br /> <br /> Though as an aside I do have to admit why noetic powers are organized as Aptitudes for people who have no ingrained restriction on what they could intrigues me on a setting story level. <br /> <br /> Two other points. <br /> <br /> 1. I too would really like the idea of having an Aberrant expansion like the one we got for Aeon. (Honestly, I would have preferred that to the wrestling book we are getting as that element of Aberrant never interested me at all.) How to represent novas through history and during both high powered and lower powered periods would be cool. Maybe even having an option for a Nova type that is more organized in their power system. <br /> <br /> 2. I REALLY want Adventure! to come out as I really really like the Stalwart, Mesmerist, Daredevil type power splats. There is so much potential in such structured gaming. <br /> <br /> Related to the above, when Adventure! comes out I REALLY hope that an expansion is present which could be titled as 'Inspired in the Modern Day' and it could talk about a modern world where instead of Novas appearing (or Psiads appearing) we get Inspired again. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I do have to re comment on my whole thought that Superiors really do need more Scale boosting powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T14:52:41-07:00","id":1336101,"title":"","content":"If I were to rewrite Superiors Using Aberrant rules I would write them as Q1 Tier 2 Novas that can buy only 1 dot Mega Attributes and Mega Edges that don\u2019t affect anything directly other than the Superior himself (besides having a limit of Q1 and Mega Attributes 1). That would be the rules for Superiors on Aberrant terms.<br /> <br /> The rules for Superiors are the ones described on Aexpansion and are based in the Aeon system and not on the Aberrant system, that was what I meant by Aeon Rules. Those rules are complete as far as they can be and describe the Superiors in a way they deserve (I would add more powers, because UNLIMITED POWER!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T15:28:24-07:00","id":1336107,"title":"","content":"I'm actually really glad that the Superiors are stated up with their own power system rather then using notes like &quot;Superiors have Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges&quot;. Instead they created new Powers using a dot system which is awesome. That power system, though needing more individual powers as everything needs more powers, is too me spectacularly amazingly awesome. <br /> <br /> That said I am also a fan of the fact that Psiads are actually stated up by saying &quot;just use Aeon for powers&quot; since rewriting a whole hundred pages of noetic powers seem like a waste. <br /> <br /> Unrelated but related I do have to say I wish we had more Mega-Edges because there seem to be areas that the old 1e Enhancements covered that 2de doesn't, and that is a pity as those categories were brilliant to me. I LOVED going through the Enhancement chapter and getting new ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T21:53:31-07:00","id":1336151,"title":"","content":"When page 88 refers to combining powers - do Psiads gain the bonuses described on page 208 of the Aeon Core from their multiple Aptitudes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T01:10:12-07:00","id":1336165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1336151#post1336151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When page 88 refers to combining powers - do Psiads gain the bonuses described on page 208 of the Aeon Core from their multiple Aptitudes?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I think the text is reasonably clear on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T03:31:53-07:00","id":1336174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1335564-aeon-aexpansion?p=1336165#post1336165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. I think the text is reasonably clear on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>it probably is, but I haven\u2019t had a chance to play test Aeon like I have Trinity Core, and the Psi rules are less intuitive for me accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-17-2019, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T04:26:21-07:00","id":1336180,"title":"","content":